reconstructed the helper protocol (contracts/helper-protocol-delta.md "Frames", research D-2, D-7) as ClientHelper writes it for op=clusterNodes, request details=node1.
The members of ok.frames, then the first 500 entries of a node information with more entries: the helper's cap of 500 detail frames stopped them (details ok 500 true; about 51 KB, below the 256 KiB budget). The ClassPath value is cut at 4,000 characters (token cut); the SystemProperties.example.property.<n> entries are invented filler. Not recorded: written by hand with the fixed nonce of the 020/021 fixtures and the two log4j lines of fixtures/server-log/v8_1/webservice/ok.frames; all names and values are fictitious (node1, node2, zone-a, 10.0.0.11:7800, /opt/inubit/...), the form of the version, the node id and the uptime is invented.
